  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rushville was named after the nearby Rush Creek, giving the town its distinctive name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rushville%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Rushville was platted in 1885 when the Fremont, Elkhorn, and Missouri Valley Railway reached the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rushville%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In Lakota, Rushville is called Owátȟokšu, meaning “Transportation City,” reflecting its historic role as a travel hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rushville%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historic landmarks include the 1904 Sheridan County Courthouse and the 1914 Gourley Opera House, both celebrated for their classic architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://rushvillene.com/explore-rushville/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1890 Armstrong House Museum, run by the Sheridan County Historical Society, preserves artifacts that chronicle the region’s pioneer past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://rushvillene.com/explore-rushville/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "As the county seat, Rushville hosts Sheridan County’s government offices and serves as the administrative hub for the surrounding Sandhills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
